    "text": "I reported incident 2 as `platform_scheduler` with 0.6 confidence. The Airflow scheduler is not heartbeating, so nothing is being scheduled.\n\n- **Evidence:** The incident shows the last heartbeat was 214 s ago, against a 90 s limit. The only scheduler events in `dip-airflow` are the `airflow-scheduler` Deployment scaling from 1 to 0 replicas and its pod being killed, both dated 2026-10-21. There are no OOM, credential or scheduling-failure signals.\n- **Confidence is limited:** That scale-down is a month before this incident, so it may not be what is happening now. Prometheus is not configured on this server, so I could not check alerts or metrics. The intake DAG shows no runs.\n- **Proposed steps (runbook 09-scheduler-down, nothing run):**\n  1. Check the Deployment's current replica count first.\n  2. If it is at 0, scale it back to 1.\n  3. If the pod is OOMKilled or crash-looping, read its previous log and raise the memory limit.\n  4. Wait for the next platform-check run to close the incident. Waiting files are picked up by their next scheduled intake run.",
